From 91db84767a35f45d0d128a128f7407964fc75b1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm: verisilicon: shadow the fbdev console
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After switching the scanout allocation back to consistent DMA, fbcon
writes directly to a write-combined buffer.  PineTab-V rotates fbcon by
90 degrees, so drawing one glyph performs many small, strided writes.
This makes boot text appear dragged and can make the console unusably slow.

Give framebuffers the standard atomic dirty callback.  drm_fbdev_dma then
selects its generic cached vmalloc shadow and copies damaged rectangles to
the consistent DMA scanout object.  Normal DRM clients such as Mutter keep
using the same consistent GEM DMA buffers; the callback does not recreate
the unsafe non-coherent allocation removed previously.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_drm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_drm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_drm.c
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ static const struct drm_driver vs_drm_driver = {
 };
 
 static const struct drm_mode_config_funcs vs_mode_config_funcs = {
-	.fb_create		= drm_gem_fb_create,
+	.fb_create		= drm_gem_fb_create_with_dirty,
 	.atomic_check		= drm_atomic_helper_check,
 	.atomic_commit		= drm_atomic_helper_commit,
 };
